-/-- Let `L/ℚ_p` be generated by a primitive root of order `p ^ f - 1`.
-The unramified cyclotomic theorem identifies `L` with the unramified extension of degree
-`f`; consequently its norm subgroup is `⟨p ^ f⟩ × U¹`.
-
-The proof compares the complete-DVF valuation with the spectral valuation
-used by the unramified norm theorem.  Uniqueness of the
-extended valuation on the finite separable extension transports
-ramification index one between the two presentations. -/
